WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. Although his family's council flat in St John's Wood, North London was compact, Charles Frantz always opened the door to his good friend Jim Ryan whenever Jim needed a place to stay. Wednesday, August 30, 1961 was one such occasion.
我们的节目涉及严重且往往令人痛心的事件。如果您在任何时候觉得需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关获取保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您使用的应用程序上或我们网站上的本期节目说明。尽管查尔斯·弗兰茨（Charles Frantz）位于伦敦北部圣约翰伍德（St John's Wood）的家族市政公寓面积不大，但每当吉姆·瑞安（Jim Ryan）需要地方住时，查尔斯总是会为这位好朋友敞开大门。1961年8月30日星期三就是这样一个日子。

2
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:32.000
24-year-old Jim slept on the sofa in the sitting room, as he did every time he visited. Although the Frantz family didn't know much about Jim's background, he was an exceptional house guest, tidy, polite and friendly. Charles' wife Charlotte thought of Jim as a son. Her three daughters called him uncle and loved when he came to stay, as he spoiled them with chocolates, flowers and pocket money. During his most recent stay, Jim Ryan joined Charles and Charlotte Frantz in the sitting room where the couple were watching television.
24岁的吉姆睡在起居室的沙发上，就像他每次来访时一样。虽然弗兰茨一家对吉姆的背景了解不多，但他是一位极好的客人，爱干净、礼貌又友善。查尔斯的妻子夏洛特（Charlotte）把吉姆当成儿子看待。她的三个女儿叫他叔叔，并且很喜欢他来做客，因为他总是用巧克力、鲜花和零花钱宠着她们。在吉姆最近的一次做客期间，他加入了坐在起居室看电视的查尔斯和夏洛特的行列。

3
00:01:32.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Suddenly, an alert flashed on the screen. Police were seeking an unidentified man for questioning in relation to a murder that had occurred the week prior. The alert was accompanied by a composite sketch known as an identikit of the wanted man. The identikit image showed a man with a pale face, slicked back dark hair, deep-set brown eyes and bushy eyebrows. His right eyebrow was raised, giving him a somewhat inquisitive expression. While studying the sketch, Charlotte Frantz remarked that it looked like her house guest
突然，屏幕上闪过一则警报。警方正在寻找一名身份不明的男子进行讯问，以配合调查一周前发生的一起谋杀案。警报伴随着一张被称为“特征拼图”（identikit）的通缉犯合成素描。拼图显示，该男子面色苍白，梳着向后服帖的黑发，深陷的棕色眼睛，浓密的眉毛。他的右眉高挑，给人一种略带探究的表情。夏洛特·弗兰茨在研究这幅素描时，评论说它看起来很像他们的客房留宿者……

4
00:02:12.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Jim Ryan, the only exception being that Jim had blue eyes. Jim heard Charlotte, but said nothing, keeping his eyes affixed to the television. A week earlier, on August 22, 1961, Michael Gregston and his girlfriend Valerie Storey took a seat inside their favourite pub, the Old Station Inn. After ordering a pint for them both, Michael spread a map out on their tabletop. The couple worked for the Rhodes Research Laboratory. 36-year-old Michael was a research scientist and 22-year-old Valerie was an assistant. That night, they were organising a car rally for their work social club.
吉姆·瑞安，唯一的区别是吉姆长着蓝色的眼睛。吉姆听到了夏洛特的话，但什么也没说，眼睛始终盯着电视。一周前的1961年8月22日，迈克尔·格雷格斯顿（Michael Gregston）和他的女朋友瓦莱丽·斯托里（Valerie Storey）坐在他们最喜欢的酒吧“老车站客栈”（Old Station Inn）里。在为两人各点了一品脱啤酒后，迈克尔在桌上摊开了一张地图。两人都在罗兹研究实验室（Rhodes Research Laboratory）工作。36岁的迈克尔是一名研究科学家，22岁的瓦莱丽是一名助理。那天晚上，他们正在为工作社交俱乐部组织一场汽车拉力赛。

5
00:03:29.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Being car fanatics, this was a task that suited them both. Along with their love of cars, Michael and Valerie shared many other things in common such as music, theatre and their work. Yet, the couple's relationship was not without controversy. Michael was married to another woman with whom he had two children. The Gregston marriage was rocky. Despite numerous attempts, Michael was unable to patch things up with his wife. He met Valerie Storey at work and the two quickly developed feelings for one another.
作为汽车狂热爱好者，这项任务非常适合他们。除了对汽车的热爱，迈克尔和瓦莱丽还有许多共同点，比如音乐、戏剧和工作。然而，两人的关系并非没有争议。迈克尔已婚，并与妻子育有两个孩子。格雷格斯顿的婚姻并不稳定。尽管多次尝试，迈克尔仍无法与妻子重修旧好。他在工作中遇到了瓦莱丽·斯托里，两人很快对彼此产生了感情。

6
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:49.000
As that relationship escalated, Michael moved out of his family home to a flat in Windsor, just west of London. He and Valerie planned to marry once Michael was officially divorced. Michael's wife was aware of the affair and didn't approve, refusing to grant her husband a divorce to remarry. Michael was certain she would come around eventually. Both he and Valerie couldn't wait to spend the rest of their lives together. At 9pm, Michael and Valerie left the old station in, in Michael's grey 1956 Morris
随着这段关系的升级，迈克尔搬出了家族住宅，搬到了伦敦正西面温莎（Windsor）的一间公寓里。他和瓦莱丽计划在迈克尔正式离婚后结婚。迈克尔的妻子知道这段婚外情并且不予认同，拒绝批准丈夫离婚以便其再婚。迈克尔确信她最终会回心转意。他和瓦莱丽都迫不及待地想要共度余生。晚上9点，迈克尔和瓦莱丽驾驶着迈克尔灰色的1956款莫里斯……

7
00:04:49.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Miner. They drove towards Slough, a town 30km west of central London. The summer evening was just beginning to get dark when the couple turned down a long lane off the A4 highway that led to a cornfield. Pitcher-esque and secluded, the cornfield served as a lover's lane for couples. Michael and Valerie visited the area often. On occasion, they'd wandered down to the adjacent River Thames. On this night, they remained in the Morris Miner.
莫里斯矿工（Morris Miner）汽车离开了老车站客栈。他们向斯劳（Slough）方向驶去，那是一个位于伦敦市中心以西30公里的小镇。当两人拐入A4公路旁一条通往玉米地的长长小道时，夏日的傍晚刚刚开始变暗。这片玉米地风景优美且偏僻，是情侣们的约会胜地。迈克尔和瓦莱丽经常光顾这个地区。有时，他们会漫步到附近的泰晤士河畔。而今晚，他们留在了莫里斯矿工汽车里。

8
00:05:25.000 --> 00:06:08.000
Unlike previous visits, there were no other cars in sight. Approximately half an hour later, Michael and Valerie heard a loud tap on the driver's side window. Outside was a man. He signalled for Michael to wind down his window. He then poked the barrel of a .38 caliber revolver through the opening. The man was immaculately dressed in a clean and crisp dark suit, white shirt and tie. His face was partially concealed by a handkerchief tied over his nose and mouth.
与以往的访问不同，视线内没有其他汽车。大约半小时后，迈克尔和瓦莱丽听到驾驶座一侧的车窗被大声敲击。外面站着一个男人。他示意迈克尔摇下车窗。随后，他将一支.38口径左轮手枪的枪管从缝隙中捅了进来。这名男子衣着无可挑剔，穿着干净利落的深色西装、白衬衫和领带。他的脸被一块系在鼻子和嘴上的手帕半遮掩着。

9
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:49.000
Valerie scoffed, thinking it was a joke. But Michael was noticeably concerned. He did as the man asked and handed him his keys so he could unlock the back door. Taking a seat inside, the hijacker told them in a thick, cockney accent, This is a hold up, I am a desperate man, I've been on the run for four months, if you do as I tell you, you will be alright. The man told the couple that he hadn't shot anyone before. Animated and excited, he said he felt like a cowboy pulling off a stun.
瓦莱丽嗤之以鼻，以为这只是个玩笑。但迈克尔明显感到担忧。他照那男人的要求做了，把钥匙递给对方以便其打开后门。劫持者坐进车内，用一口浓重的伦敦东区口音对他们说：“这是一场抢劫，我是个绝望的人，我已经逃亡了四个月，如果你照我的话做，你们就会没事。”这名男子告诉这对情侣，他以前没有枪击过任何人。他情绪激动、兴奋地说道，他感觉自己像个干了一票惊天大案的牛仔。

10
00:06:49.000 --> 00:07:19.000
Michael and Valerie annoyed the hijacker. They kept asking what he wanted, to which he replied in a half. It's alright, there's no hurry. He ordered Michael to drive further into the cornfield. It was now pitch black. The air was still. On the man's order, Michael killed the engine and the lights. Every time Michael or Valerie attempted to glance at the stranger in the back seat,
迈克尔和瓦莱丽惹恼了劫持者。他们不断追问他想要什么，而他则含糊其辞地回答：“没事，不着急。”他命令迈克尔把车开进玉米地深处。此时外面漆黑一片。空气静止不动。在男人的命令下，迈克尔熄灭了发动机和车灯。每当迈克尔或瓦莱丽试图看一眼后座的陌生人时……

11
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:59.000
he ordered them to look straight ahead. The man made small talk as the trio sat in the car. He inquired about Michael and Valerie's relationship and asked if they were married. In return, he told them about himself. He revealed that he had been in institutions or remand homes since he was eight years old. Nearly an hour later, at 10.30, there was movement at a house nearby. The trio watched as a man emerged from the property's back door. They wondered whether he would spot the Morris minor in the cornfield.
他就会命令他们目视前方。三个人坐在车里时，这名男子闲聊了起来。他打听迈克尔和瓦莱丽的关系，问他们是否结婚。作为回报，他向他们讲述了自己的情况。他透露，自己从八岁起就一直在收容所或拘留所里度过。将近一个小时后的10点30分，附近的一所房子有了动静。三人看着一个男人从该房产的后门走了出来。他们纳闷对方是否会发现玉米地里的莫里斯矿工汽车。

12
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:37.000
The gunman warned Michael and Valerie not to say anything if he happened to approach. Moments later, the man walked back inside and closed the door. At 11.30pm, nearly two hours since the ordeal began, the gunman's hunger got the better of him. He ordered Michael out of the car and to the vehicle's boot. Taking a blanket down so his hostage would be comfortable, he instructed Michael to get in. Michael pleaded with the man, telling him that there was an exhaust leak that allowed fumes
持枪歹徒警告迈克尔和瓦莱丽，如果他碰巧走过来，千万不要出声。片刻之后，那名男子走回屋内并关上了门。晚上11点30分，距离这场磨难开始已经将近两个小时，歹徒的饥饿感占了上风。他命令迈克尔下车并走到汽车后备箱。他放下一条毯子以便人质能舒服些，并指示迈克尔钻进去。迈克尔向男子恳求，告诉他车上有排气泄漏，废气会漏进……

13
00:08:37.000 --> 00:09:15.000
into the boot. He would surely die if confined in the small space for a period of time. The hijacker agreed that this was a bad idea. Instead, he forced Michael to drive the car towards London, approximately an hour's drive away. On the journey, the man told Michael to pull over at a milk machine. However, nobody had a sixpence to make a purchase, so they continued on. What should have been a 28-mile journey east soon became a drive all over the English countryside.
后备箱里。如果在这个小空间里待上一段时间，他必死无疑。劫持者同意这是一个糟糕的主意。相反，他强迫迈克尔把车开向伦敦，大约有一个小时的车程。在旅途中，这名男子让迈克尔在自动售奶机旁靠边停车。然而，谁也没有六便士硬币来购买，于是他们继续前行。原本只需向东行驶28英里的行程，很快变成了一场横跨英国乡村的漫游。

14
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:45.000
The man spoke nearly non-stop. Eventually, the fuel warning light came on, and Michael pulled the Morris Miner into a garage. He approached the elderly pump attendant, asking if he could put two gallons into the tank. He tried to covertly alert the attendant to what was happening in the car, but failed to do so. The trio drove on to Stanmore, moving away from London.
这个男人几乎说个不停。最终，燃油警告灯亮了，迈克尔把莫里斯矿工汽车开进了一家修理厂。他走到年迈的加油工身旁，询问是否能在油箱里加两加仑油。他试图借此暗中向加油工警示车内正在发生的事情，但未能成功。三人继续驱车前往远离伦敦的斯坦莫尔（Stanmore）。

15
00:09:45.000 --> 00:10:21.000
There, the hijacker spotted a cigarette machine. He didn't usually smoke, but ordered Michael out and watched as he walked across the road to purchase a pack. Instead of making a run for it, Michael returned to the car, presumably so Valerie wasn't left alone with the man. The traffic had thinned considerably by the time the three drove north to St Albans and further north towards Luton. The Morris Miner then hit the A6 motorway, heading towards Bedford, approximately 60
在那里，劫持者发现了一台香烟自动售货机。他平时不抽烟，但命令迈克尔下车，并看着他过马路去买一包。迈克尔并没有趁机逃跑，而是回到了车里，大概是为了不让瓦莱丽独自一人和这个男人呆在一起。当三人向北驶向圣奥尔本斯（St Albans）并进一步向北驶向卢顿（Luton）时，交通已经明显减少了。莫里斯矿工汽车随后驶上了A6高速公路，向距离伦敦以北约60英里的贝德福德（Bedford）驶去。

16
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:56.000
miles north of London. By this stage, the man was tired and needed to rest. It was nearing 1.30am. He looked out the rear window for somewhere suitable to stop. He ordered Michael to pull over twice so he could, quote, kip a slang word for a nap. Both times, he changed his mind. As they continued past the small village of Clophill and Upper Hill, the man saw the perfect place to stop.
此时，这个男人已经累了，需要休息。时间将近凌晨1点30分。他望向后车窗寻找适合停车的地方。他两次命令迈克尔停车，以便他“小睡”（kip，俚语意为小睡）。但两次他都改变了主意。当他们驶过克洛菲尔（Clophill）和上希尔（Upper Hill）的小村庄时，这个男人找到了完美的停车地点。

17
00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:38.000
He told Michael to pull off into a lay-by alongside the road. Michael didn't want to, but eventually relented. His nerves were understandable. Anyone passing by could see the name of the area printed on a sign in flashing lights. Dead Man's Hill The man told Michael and Valerie he would have to tie them up while he had a kip. He took Michael and the pair searched the boot for a suitable material to use as a restraint. If they were able to find anything, they returned to the car.
他告诉迈克尔将车开到路边的一处紧急停车湾。迈克尔本不想这么做，但最终还是妥协了。他的紧张是可以理解的。任何路过的人都能看到印在闪烁灯光招牌上的地名——“死人山”（Dead Man's Hill）。这名男子告诉迈克尔和瓦莱丽，在他小睡期间他必须把他们绑起来。他带着迈克尔在后备箱里搜寻适合用作束缚物的材料。他们找到了一些东西后，便回到了车里。

18
00:11:38.000 --> 00:12:17.000
The man ended up tying Valerie's hands using Michael's tie. They pleaded with him not to kill them. He reassured the couple, if I was going to shoot you, I would have done it before now. The man then noticed a duffel bag of laundry in the front seat. He asked Michael to pick it up and pass it over. As Michael reached down, the man shot him twice at point-blank range. One bullet entered his left ear, the other his left cheek. Michael slumped over.
这名男子最终用迈克尔的领带绑住了瓦莱丽的双手。他们恳求他不要杀他们。他安慰这对情侣说：“如果我要枪击你们，我之前就已经这么做了。”接着，男子注意到前座上有一个装有换洗衣物的国民服役帆布袋（duffel bag）。他让迈克尔把它拿起来递过来。正当迈克尔弯腰去拿时，这名男子在极近的距离向他开了两枪。一颗子弹射入他的左耳，另一颗射入他的左脸颊。迈克尔瘫倒在地。

19
00:12:17.000 --> 00:13:11.000
Valerie screamed, you shot him you bastard, why did you do that? To which the man replied, he frightened me, he moved too quick and I got frightened. As Valerie sobbed, the man warned, be quiet will you, I'm trying to think. They argued for nearly 20 minutes as to whether Michael should receive medical attention. The man then removed the handkerchief from his face and ordered Valerie to kiss him. When she refused, he threatened her with his gun, saying, I will count five. As Valerie turned to kiss her attacker, a truck drove by. For a few seconds, the man's face was illuminated by the passing headlights.
瓦莱丽尖叫道：“你开枪打了他，你这个混蛋，你为什么要这么做？”对此，男子回答道：“他吓到我了，他动得太快，我被吓到了。”在瓦莱丽的啜泣声中，男子警告道：“安静点好吗，我在思考。”他们争论了近20分钟，讨论是否应该让迈克尔接受医疗救治。随后，男子扯下脸上的手帕，命令瓦莱丽吻他。当她拒绝时，他用枪威胁她，说道：“我数到五。”正当瓦莱丽转过身去吻她的袭击者时，一辆卡车驶过。几秒钟内，男子的脸被驶过的前灯照亮。

20
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:51.000
The man ordered Valerie into the back seat. He covered Michael's face with a rag before raping Valerie. A few other cars passed, but none for long enough that Valerie could get another good look at the man's face. When he was finished, Valerie asked the man to take the car and drive away. He reassured her that he was in no hurry. He needed to get rid of Michael's body and asked Valerie to help him. Together, they dragged Michael from the car, dumping him by the side of the road.
这名男子命令瓦莱丽坐到后座。他用一块抹布盖住迈克尔的脸，然后强暴了瓦莱丽。又有几辆车驶过，但没有一辆停留足够长的时间让瓦莱丽能够再次看清男子的脸。完事后，瓦莱丽要求男子开着车离开。他安慰她，说自己并不着急。他需要处理掉迈克尔的尸体，并要求瓦莱丽帮他。他们合力把迈克尔从车里拖出来，扔在了路边。

21
00:13:51.000 --> 00:14:31.000
The man then ordered Valerie to show him how to start the Morris Miner and change its gears. Twice he stalled, and twice Valerie had to show him how to restart the engine. Eventually, he hopped out of the driver's seat, leaving the engine running. It was 3.30am. Valerie handed him a £1 note from her raincoat and pleaded for the man to just go. He replied he would have to hit her over the head or something. He begged to be left unharmed. The man seemingly relented.
接着，男子命令瓦莱丽教他如何启动莫里斯矿工汽车以及如何换挡。他熄火了两次，瓦莱丽不得不两次教他如何重新启动发动机。最终，他跳下驾驶座，任由发动机继续运转。当时是凌晨3点30分。瓦莱丽从雨衣里递给他一张1英镑的纸币，恳求他赶紧走。他回答说，他可能得敲晕她的头或者干点别的。她哀求对方放过自己，不要伤害她。男子似乎心软了。

22
00:14:31.000 --> 00:15:19.000
He turned away and walked back towards the car. When he was about six feet from Valerie, he turned suddenly and fired several bullets at her. Valerie fell to her knees and then to the ground, coming to rest next to Michael's body. The man reloaded and shot at Valerie another three times. He calmly took the driver's seat of the Morris Miner and sped off towards London. That morning of Wednesday, August 23, 1961, began as a normal workday for engineering foreman James Skillett.
他转过身，朝汽车走去。当他离瓦莱丽大约六英尺远时，他突然转身，朝她连开数枪。瓦莱丽双膝跪地，随后倒在地上，倒在了迈克尔尸体的旁边。男子重新装弹，又朝瓦莱丽开 了三枪。他平静地坐上莫里斯矿工汽车的驾驶座，向伦敦方向疾驰而去。1961年8月23日星期三的那个早晨，对工程工长詹姆斯·斯基利特（James Skillett）来说，原本只是一个普通的工作日。

23
00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:56.000
He picked up a friend as usual, and the two travelled together in his car towards the town of Stratford, heading towards London. As they pulled up to a set of traffic lights in the eastern London town of Wilford, they noticed a car being driven erratically. It was a grey Morris Miner. The car swerved in its lane, narrowly missing James's car as it sped past. A crunching sound could be heard as the driver of the Morris Miner changed gears and dodged further vehicles approaching from the opposite lane.
他像往常一样接上了一个朋友，两人开着车一起朝斯特拉特福（Stratford）镇进发，驶向伦敦。当他们将车开到伦敦东部威尔福德（Wilford）的一个红绿灯路口时，他们注意到一辆汽车正在行车不稳地行驶着。那是一辆灰色的莫里斯矿工汽车。这辆车在车道上左右摇晃，在疾驰而过时差点撞上詹姆斯的车。随着莫里斯矿工汽车的司机换档并躲避从对向车道驶来的更多车辆，可以听到一阵刺耳的金属摩擦声。

