In Maidervale, West London, hotel manager Robert Crocker was busy inspecting the rooms of the Vienna Hotel. Robert arrived at room 24, a large basement room with multiple beds. It was unoccupied at the time. Robert gave it the once over, looking for anything out of place or missing. On one of the armchairs next to a single bed were two 38-caliber cartridge cases. Robert's first thought was to simply throw them away, but he decided to call his local police and report the finding.
在伦敦西部麦达维尔（Maida Vale），酒店经理罗伯特·克罗克（Robert Crocker）正忙着检查维也纳酒店（Vienna Hotel）的房间。罗伯特来到了24号房，这是一间有多张床铺的大型地下室房间。当时里面没有人。罗伯特粗略检查了一遍，看是否有东西放错地方或丢失。单人床旁边的一把扶手椅上放着两个.38口径弹壳。罗伯特最初的想法是直接把它们扔掉，但他最终还是决定打电话给当地警方报告这一发现。

